  "counterarguments_and_limits": [
    "A larger outer timeout can prolong runner occupation and a later cancellation. Preserve strict per-probe timeouts, process exits, missing-artifact rejection and all mandatory result checks.",
    "The ten Discovery per-call caps sum to 60:30. Adding the maximum allowed durations of every other stage can still exceed a 120-minute outer limit. The proposed 120 minutes is evidence-based capacity, not a proof of worst-case schedulability.",
    "The current Native gate took 45:04 versus 39:03 in the older reference. The older 64:35 whole build cannot be treated as a fixed baseline.",
    "The dominant new capture took 773.477093322 seconds of its unchanged 900-second individual allowance. Increasing the outer budget does not cure an individual probe timeout; do not relax that gate.",
    "Cache state, source, runner load, APK build duration and artifact work differ between the cited runs. Actual combined completion remains a future CI observation.",
    "Two existing delivery source tests literally require 90 minutes and must be explicitly changed with the separate Root budget patch; otherwise the desired workflow change will correctly fail those source contracts. All their other assertions should remain unchanged.",
    "The active Host3d run and the frozen five-file Village integration review remain unchanged; this document authorizes no ref movement, rerun or acceptance transfer."
  ],
